{
  "title": "Florence Doors",
  "indexDescription": "Florence doors from a random street.",
  "description": "Agatha found a highly rated small restaurant in Florence. The place was full when we got there. They gave us some prosecco while we waited outside for a table. \n\nI wandered around the quiet narrow street and took pictures of the doors for this collection. \n\nI think it is interesting the beauty and variety of the doors from a random small street in Florence.\n\nThe restaurant is called Cantinetta delle Terme.  Cantinetta  means“small wine bar” and the street is called VIA DELLE TERME.\n\nThere are no end to supper fancy large doors throughout the city, some gold plated, with all the churches and cathedrals.",
